Backport of wlroots commit 08a9f9f14fc8fd173d1768588699d2e152b6cde6
("xwayland/xwm: fix association/map race", Isaac Freund), rebased onto 0.20.2.
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wlroots/wlroots/-/commit/08a9f9f14fc8fd173d1768588699d2e152b6cde6

Without it, an X11 window whose first buffer commit reaches the compositor
before its WL_SURFACE_SERIAL message is paired but never mapped, so Sway never
shows it.

TODO: Remove once nixpkgs' wlroots_0_20 is a release that includes 08a9f9f1.
0.20.2 does not; no release included it when this patch was added.

--- a/xwayland/xwm.c
+++ b/xwayland/xwm.c
@@ -1237,6 +1237,14 @@
 	}
 
 	wl_signal_emit_mutable(&xsurface->events.associate, NULL);
+
+	// Wlroots communicates with Xwayland over both an X11 socket and a Wayland
+	// socket with no synchronization between the two. There is no guarantee that
+	// e.g. the WL_SURFACE_SERIAL X11 client message will be received on the X11
+	// socket before the first buffer attach/commit on the Wayland socket.
+	if (wlr_surface_has_buffer(surface)) {
+		wlr_surface_map(surface);
+	}
 }
 
 static void xwm_handle_create_notify(struct wlr_xwm *xwm,
